---
/**
 * Written against what this site actually does, which is very little: it is a
 * static site with no forms, no accounts, no analytics and no cookies of its
 * own. A boilerplate policy describing data collection that does not happen
 * would be inaccurate in the one document whose whole purpose is accuracy.
 *
 * Two things here WILL need editing if the site changes:
 *   - add an analytics provider, and the third-party section has to say so
 *   - add a contact form, and the whole of section 2 changes
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MediaHeader from '../components/MediaHeader.astro';
import { PAGE_SEO, PRACTICE, DOCTOR } from '../consts';
import { MAIL_HREF } from '../lib/practice-links';

const trail = [{ name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy-policy' }];
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={PAGE_SEO.privacy.title}
  description={PAGE_SEO.privacy.description}
  breadcrumbs={trail}
>
  <MediaHeader
    trail={trail}
    title="Privacy"
    titleEm="policy"
    size="md"
    lede={`How this website handles information, and how confidentiality is treated at the practice. Last updated ${updated}.`}
  />

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;" aria-label="Privacy policy">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="rich" data-reveal-group>
        <h2 data-reveal>1. Who this applies to</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          This policy covers this website, published on behalf of {DOCTOR.name},
          {DOCTOR.jobTitle}. It does not cover the websites of
          {PRACTICE.affiliation} or of any other organisation this site links to. Those
          have their own policies, and their own practices.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>2. What this website collects</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Nothing that identifies you. This is a static website. It has no contact form, no
          login, no comments, no newsletter signup and no shopping basket, so there is no
          mechanism here through which you could submit personal information to us even if
          you wanted to.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal>
          The site sets no cookies of its own and runs no analytics or advertising trackers.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>3. What the hosting provider records</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          As with any website, the server that delivers these pages keeps standard technical
          logs. These typically include your IP address, the time of the request, the page
          requested, and your browser's user-agent string. That data is generated by the
          hosting infrastructure for security and reliability, is not used by us to build a
          profile of you, and is not combined with anything else.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>4. Third-party content on these pages</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Two things on this site are loaded from other companies, and each sees the request
          your browser makes for it:
        </p>
        <ul data-reveal>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Maps.</strong> The booking and contact pages embed a map. Google
            receives the request that loads it, and its own privacy policy governs what it
            does with that. The map is inert until you click it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Fonts.</strong> The two typefaces used across the site are
            requested from Google's font service when a page loads.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p data-reveal>
          Neither is used by us to identify or track visitors, and neither is given any
          information about you beyond the request itself.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>5. Contacting the practice</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          If you telephone, send a WhatsApp message or write to
          <a href={MAIL_HREF}>{PRACTICE.email}</a>, what you send is held by the person or
          the service you sent it to. Email and WhatsApp are convenient but they are not
          secure channels, and neither is a suitable place for detailed medical information.
          Please keep messages brief and arrange an appointment for anything clinical.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>6. Patient confidentiality</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Medical records and anything you disclose in a consultation are governed by
          medical confidentiality and by the record-keeping policies of
          {PRACTICE.affiliation}, not by this website. What you say in the consulting room
          stays there. The narrow exceptions, where there is an immediate risk to your
          safety or to someone else's, are explained at the first appointment.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal>
          Nothing said in a consultation appears on this website, and no patient is
          identified anywhere on it.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>7. Children</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          This site is written for adults, and for the parents and guardians of the
          adolescents seen at the practice. It does not knowingly collect information from
          anyone, of any age.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          If the site gains a contact form, analytics, or any other feature that changes the
          answers above, this page will be updated before that feature goes live, and the
          date at the top will change with it.
        </p>

        <h2 data-reveal>9. Questions</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Write to <a href={MAIL_HREF}>{PRACTICE.email}</a>, or ask at your appointment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
